cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "flood-policy-kit: NUTS3 river flood exposure for Europe, from the JRC hazard maps to a policy brief"
abstract: >-
  A screening toolkit that computes the population exposed to river flooding in
  each of the 1,345 NUTS3 regions of Europe for nine return periods (RP10 to
  RP500), by combining the JRC river flood hazard maps with the GHS-POP population
  grid, and qualifies each figure with the Member States' Article 5 declarations
  served by the EEA, the WFD river basin districts and the Copernicus CDS river
  discharge projections. It ships a Streamlit and a React choropleth, a JSON API,
  a grounded cite-or-refuse drafting workflow over a sourced policy corpus with a
  human approval gate, and a policy answer built around Directive 2007/60/EC; it
  is not a substitute for the statutory flood hazard and risk maps reported by
  the Member States under that Directive.
authors:
